[[File:SWBET_T16Skyhopper_MarkMolnar.jpg|thumb|right|180px|A skyhopper in flight]]
'''Skyhoppers''' were a type of [[repulsorlift]] vehicles built primarily for pleasure and sport flying. However, paramilitary forces and [[Law enforcement agency|law enforcement agencies]] occasionally used armed and lightly [[armor]]ed skyhoppers for reconnaissance and patrol.<ref name="S&S">''[[Starships and Speeders]]''</ref>

During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Mimbanese]] [[Kierah Koovah|Kierah "Gunny" Koovah]] flew a skyhopper at the [[Battle of Mimban]]. She was shot down by enemy [[Separatist Droid Army|Separatist forces]] while attempting to reach [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[Clone trooper|clone]] forces, and lost her left arm as a result.<ref name="Squadrons">''[[Star Wars: Squadrons]]''</ref>

While living on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]], the [[moisture farmer]] [[Luke Skywalker]] tinkered with skyhoppers and [[landspeeder]]s.<ref name="Weapon of the Jedi">''[[The Weapon of a Jedi: A Luke Skywalker Adventure]]''</ref> Tatooine youngsters, such as Luke Skywalker and [[Biggs Darklighter]],<ref name="ANH:PSF">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref> raced their modified skyhoppers and landspeeders in [[Beggar's Canyon]] near [[Mos Espa]] on non-[[podracing]] [[Standard day|days]]. Speeding through the winding canyon with lightly armed [[repulsorcraft]] models such as<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> the [[T-16 skyhopper]],<ref name="ANH:PSF" /> youngsters dreamt of becoming [[Homeworld|hometown]] heroes<ref name="CL2016" /> as they [[Pneumatic cannon|blasted]] the native [[womp rat]]s.<ref name="ANH:PSF" />

